From: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: musb: sunxi: apply a mode change while the controller is idle

Writing musb's `mode` attribute ends in sunxi_musb_set_mode(), which
records the new PHY mode in glue->phy_mode, sets PHY_MODE_PEND and leaves
phy_set_mode() to sunxi_musb_work(). The work returns at once when the
controller is not enabled, so with no gadget bound and no host session
the request is dropped. The next write of the same mode is then a no-op,
because glue->phy_mode already holds it, and the port stays where it was
with no error anywhere.

Seen on the H713 projector (kernel 0215): after unbinding the gadget,
`echo host > mode` returned success, but the PHY never left peripheral
and the port stayed routed to musb (OTGCTL bit 0 still set), so a stick
in the port was never seen by ehci0. Written while the gadget was still
bound, the same request switched at once ("Changing dr_mode to 1").

The PHY is initialised in sunxi_musb_init() and released in
sunxi_musb_exit(), which cancels this work first, so phy_set_mode() is
valid whenever the work runs. Apply a pending mode change in the
disabled case too. The enabled path is unchanged.

--- a/drivers/usb/musb/sunxi.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/musb/sunxi.c
@@ -99,8 +99,19 @@
 	struct sunxi_glue *glue = container_of(work, struct sunxi_glue, work);
 	bool vbus_on, phy_on;
 
-	if (!test_bit(SUNXI_MUSB_FL_ENABLED, &glue->flags))
+	if (!test_bit(SUNXI_MUSB_FL_ENABLED, &glue->flags)) {
+		/*
+		 * The PHY is live from sunxi_musb_init() to sunxi_musb_exit(),
+		 * which cancels this work, whether or not the controller is
+		 * enabled. A mode change written while it is disabled (a
+		 * dual-role port with no gadget bound) must still reach the
+		 * PHY, or it is lost: sunxi_musb_set_mode() has already taken
+		 * the new mode as current and will not ask again.
+		 */
+		if (test_and_clear_bit(SUNXI_MUSB_FL_PHY_MODE_PEND, &glue->flags))
+			phy_set_mode(glue->phy, glue->phy_mode);
 		return;
+	}
 
 	if (test_and_clear_bit(SUNXI_MUSB_FL_HOSTMODE_PEND, &glue->flags)) {
 		struct musb *musb = glue->musb;
